00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.139 align:start position:0%
ministers of Agriculture and Fisheries  meeting on Monday in Brussels discussed  the future of the EU milk sector  following the end of the quota system in  2015 some countries express their  concerns about potential price  volatility and asked for additional  measures to address it in particular in  the case of vulnerable milk production  areas ministers also welcomed the plans  presented by the Commission to bring  together and simplify to currently  separate school schemes the school fruit  scheme and the school milk scheme  delegations agreed that the proposed  scheme will contribute to improving  healthy eating habits among  schoolchildren it will also help to  foster link between schoolchildren and  agriculture although Member States see  the advantages of the unified scheme in  terms of public health some have doubts  that it offers a real simplification the  council also discussed the new  promotional rules for European  agricultural products which aim to open  up new markets for these products and to  increase consumer awareness of their  quality but there are different views as  to whether the new information and  promotion measures should concentrate on  the internal market or rather on the  foreign markets to avoid a distortion of  competition in the EU finally ministers  listen to the priorities of the Greek EU  presidency which include wrapping up the  work on the reformed Common Agricultural  Policy finalizing the agreement with the  European Parliament on the European  maritime and Fisheries fund and moving  ahead with the food chain legislation  package
 

